<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ahmad al-Mukarram</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">11th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ahmad al-Mukarram was the second ruler of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sulayhid-dynasty">Sulayhid dynasty</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yemen">Yemen</a>, succeeding his father Ali al-Sulayhi after Ali was killed by the Najahids in the 1060s. Afflicted by paralysis, he left much of the government to his wife Arwa, who moved the court to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jibla">Dhu Jibla</a>. After his death Arwa ruled on behalf of the dynasty for decades.</p></div>
